WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.520
- We are here with America's sweetheart,

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.700
and someone who just is the coolest person

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.045
on the planet, Jennifer Aniston.

00:00:09.045 --> 00:00:11.611
(audience cheering)

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.480
You know "The Morning Show."

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.583
- Yes.

00:00:13.583 --> 00:00:16.583
(audience cheering)

00:00:17.422 --> 00:00:18.890
- What are you channeling in that

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.160
because it's the greatest
thing I've ever seen

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.890
as an actress and in your body of work?

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.280
- It was basically about
just revisiting some

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.190
of the shadows, blind spots that I'd put

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.420
into a particular file,

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.840
and meeting them head on,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.890
and actually releasing them.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:40.280
It was like an extraordinary therapy.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.100
Better than any actual therapist
that I've been going to

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.100
for years on end 'cause.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.730
- Do you think that Alex Levy

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.660
is the closest character to you

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.800
or that you've blessed it

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.540
with some of your deepest
truths behind her?

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.240
- I think it's a little bit of both.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.410
Alex Levy is people,
someone maybe in particular

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.240
who I have witnessed in my life.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.690
People, say a combination of
people who I have watched,

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:09.160
and remember thinking I
don't wanna ever do that.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.850
I don't wanna be that.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.070
Then there is sort of
the tapping into the part

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:16.030
that wants to have that
scream into your pillow

00:01:16.030 --> 00:01:18.300
and yell, which I never was able to do

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.300
until I did it in front
of 150 crew members.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.430
- [Drew] Because you
wouldn't let yourself?

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.920
- I wouldn't let myself.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.510
I didn't know how to, I
like to discuss things,

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.910
I like to have a conversation,
a rational conversation

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.600
'cause if you're ever with
someone who's a screamer,

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.650
nothing gets done.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.940
I just just go shut down,
shut down, shut down.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.920
- What was it about
this point in your life

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.470
that you were like I've,

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.130
was it an I have nothing to lose?

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:42.820
- It's written, it was written for me,

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.220
it was written for me, it was written,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.600
we talked about it.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.414
There's a part as you get older

00:01:47.414 --> 00:01:51.927
that you just hit a wonderful
who gives a rat's (beep).

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.374
This is just my warmup.

00:01:55.374 --> 00:01:58.298
(audience clapping)

00:01:58.298 --> 00:01:59.131
It's true.

00:02:00.506 --> 00:02:01.508
Right?

00:02:01.508 --> 00:02:02.341
- Yes.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.700
I thank you for sharing
that with the world

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.060
because it's cathartic for us watching it.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:10.893
- Thank you.

00:02:10.893 --> 00:02:12.470
- I'm serious.
- Thank you.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:15.320
- I just marvel, I marvel,
I marvel, I marvel.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.460
- I can't wait to do a
comedy, let me tell you that.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:21.170
Rush me to a comedy immediately

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.180
after completing that second season.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.560
- I mean, now, when I think of hair,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.690
obviously you're the most
famous head of hair we've got.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:30.523
Seriously.

00:02:30.523 --> 00:02:31.356
- Sad.

00:02:31.356 --> 00:02:33.452
- Come on, the Rachel, hello?

00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:35.280
(audience cheering)

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.730
So when I hear that
you're doing hair care,

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.800
I'm like give it to me now.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.110
I'm on the feeder.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.210
Tell me about LolaVie.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:48.070
- It comes out of many years
of having really unruly hair.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:50.170
That's always been my struggle.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.120
I paired myself with
these wonderful people

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.570
that used to be part of Arden,

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.190
and maybe five years ago,

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.290
we started working on this,

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:59.394
and we're doing one product at a time

00:02:59.394 --> 00:03:01.950
because it has to be perfect.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.330
And that was the first one we started

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.460
'cause I live for a good detangler

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.120
'cause you rip through your hair

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.920
when it's wet, it's half the damage.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.140
- I heard a hot tip.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.660
When your hair is wet,

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.050
use a wide tooth comb

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.860
because your follicle
is at its most fragile.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:18.978
- Yes.

00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:19.811
- Please do not use a brush

00:03:19.811 --> 00:03:21.460
and break through it.

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:24.080
- Especially a really
bristly brush is death.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.660
Or there's actually wet brushes

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:27.210
that are made for wet hair.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.430
- I do love that wet brush.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:29.263
- I love a wet brush.

00:03:29.263 --> 00:03:30.096
I just discovered it.

00:03:30.096 --> 00:03:32.340
- Oh my God, I have minis for my kids.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.173
They're all over the house.

00:03:33.173 --> 00:03:34.006
- There are minis?

00:03:34.006 --> 00:03:35.930
- Yes, you can travel with them.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:36.930
- Oh God.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.544
- I'm gonna get you so many wet brushes,

00:03:38.544 --> 00:03:39.377
you're not gonna believe.

00:03:39.377 --> 00:03:41.572
- I'm just not gonna know
what to do with myself.

00:03:41.572 --> 00:03:44.155
(upbeat music)

